<div class="bb-quote"><b>Benhimself wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">Legacy, Team Leader Tachyon, Dark Visionary,&nbsp;Wraith, and Tempest. Against... pretty much anyone. Solid damage, both single-target and group, solid ongoing control, solid deck manipulation, solid damage prevention. You could come up with a better team for specific situations, sure, but if you were all &quot;Okay, you get one team and you have to face every villain, on advanced challenge mode&quot; that&#39;s what I would take, no questions asked.
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
&nbsp;We&#39;ve had the discussion about best general team elsewhere, but I&#39;m failing to resist the urge to jump into it again here because you&#39;ve put TLT on a team and then not given her the teammates that make the most of extra card draw. I&#39;m not saying your team is bad. It looks great. But TLT w/ NightMist, Scholar, Haka? Stupendous. O-X and Chronoranger are great choices, too, because of their extra card plays.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

That&#39;s a very fair point. I&#39;d probably swap out Wraith or Tempest and put Argent Adept in there, so EVERYBODY can get the benefit of extra plays.

&nbsp;

Specific matchup recommendations? For La Capitan: Sentinels and Super-Scientific Tachyon. It&#39;s almost embarassing. If you really want to get absurd, throw in, like, Grandpa Legacy and Prime Warden Fanatic and Argent Adept, or anyone who can reliably churn more powers into SST, and throw all those experiments at the Sentinels. Each one has very high odds of being two damaging one-shots, each of which gets boosted by nemesis damage if you throw them straight to the dome, and you need almost no set-up for it to work. Which is nice against her piles of card destruction.

[quote="Donner"]

I like Setback, Scholar, and Argent Adept.They weaponize heals, give cards to the Scholar so he can get 2 Mortal Form to Energy and 1 Solid to Liquid, and give extra actions.&nbsp; Argent Adept can get Cash Out back for Setback, who can risk into it, triggering Mortal Form to Energy twice for 3 damage.&nbsp; Scholar can cause Setback and Argent Adept to get extra power uses and card plays (or get Cash Out back out again!).&nbsp; They have good ongoing destruction from AA and Setback.&nbsp; And once Setback gets Wrong Time and Place, he usually has a ton of tokens and can help beat down the baddies.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

That&#39;s pretty nasty, though I don&#39;t think Setback would be my fourth. &nbsp;I&#39;d probably use Wraith. &nbsp;I love Wraith. Damage, Control and tons of draw. &nbsp;&nbsp;

Or maybe Vis/Parse. &nbsp;Still ongoing control but some villain deck control too.
